  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set tracing the exception path from Netty's channel pipeline through to Spring WebFlux's error handling:\n\n**Netty side:**\n- `AbstractChannelHandlerContext.java` \u2014 `exceptionCaught`/`fireExceptionCaught` propagation mechanics\n- `DefaultChannelPipeline.java` \u2014 pipeline-level exception dispatch to the tail context\n- `ChannelPipeline.java` / `ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 the handler contract exceptions flow through\n\n**Bridge (Spring's Reactor Netty integration):**\n- `ReactorHttpHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 adapts `HttpHandler` to reactor-netty's `BiFunction<HttpServerRequest, HttpServerResponse, Mono<Void>>`; this is where Netty-side errors first enter the Spring reactive stack (only logged via `doOnError`, not enriched)\n- `ReactorServerHttpRequest.java` / `ReactorServerHttpResponse.java` \u2014 wrap reactor-netty's request/response, the layer where low-level channel exceptions get translated into reactive-stream error signals\n\n**Spring WebFlux side:**\n- `HttpWebHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 terminal `HttpHandler`; `handleUnresolvedError()` is the key translation point that collapses any unhandled exception into a generic `500` with no original context preserved once the response is committed\n- `ExceptionHandlingWebHandler.java`, `FilteringWebHandler.java`, `WebHandlerDecorator.java` \u2014 the WebHandler decorator chain error propagation runs through before reaching `HttpWebHandlerAdapter`",
